{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3437","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3437","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3437\",\"parent_revision\":\"8023bbf5bbb5e1b0e0118c657156a9be81eeb2e411e789b012aba67e31dcabf0\",\"root_revision\":\"8023bbf5bbb5e1b0e0118c657156a9be81eeb2e411e789b012aba67e31dcabf0\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: 2026-09-06\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\ndevelopment-harness ships .codex-plugin and .cursor-plugin manifests, so it claims support for three harnesses. Its task-state tracking works on one. The claim that the other two have no subagent-stop hook is false; the real gap is payload shape and identity.\\n\\nWHAT EACH HARNESS PROVIDES\\n\\nClaude Code (https://code.claude.com/docs/en/hooks, accessed 2026-09-06): SubagentStop. Payload carries agent_id (\\\"Unique identifier for the subagent. Present only when the hook fires inside a subagent call.\\\") and agent_transcript_path. The final assistant message is not supplied; it must be read out of the transcript.\\n\\nCodex (https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/hooks, accessed 2026-09-06): SubagentStart and SubagentStop both exist. SubagentStop carries agent_id, agent_type, agent_transcript_path, and last_assistant_message (\\\"Latest subagent assistant message, if available\\\"). session_id is documented as \\\"Current Codex session id. Subagent hooks use the parent session id.\\\"\\n\\nCursor (https://cursor.com/docs/hooks, accessed 2026-09-06): subagentStop exists. Payload carries subagent_type, status, task, description, summary, duration_ms, message_count, tool_call_count, loop_count, modified_files, and agent_transcript_path (string or null). There is NO per-subagent unique identifier in the stop payload; subagent_id appears only in subagentStart. Base fields include conversation_id, which for a subagent refers to the parent session.\\n\\nCONSEQUENCES\\n\\nAll three pass the PARENT session id to a subagent hook, so the session-id correlation defect is universal rather than Claude Code specific.\\n\\nA correlation key based on agent_id resolves on Claude Code and Codex but is unresolvable on Cursor. Any key that must work on all three has to be derivable from what the dispatcher knows at write time.\\n\\nTwo of the three supply the subagent's final message in the payload (last_assistant_message, summary), so the transcript-scanning STATUS parser is a Claude-Code-shaped workaround rather than a portable mechanism.\\n\\nThe dispatcher, not the hook, should be the mechanism that reads the reported STATUS and sets task state, with each harness's hook acting as a backstop where one exists. Runtime text that describes the hook as the mechanism needs to say this.\\n\\nUNVERIFIED\\n\\nA Cursor community bug report states subagentStop never fires for background subagents and that summary, modified_files and agent_transcript_path arrive missing or null. Forum source, not documentation, and not reproduced here. If it holds, Cursor's event cannot be relied on even where it is documented.\\n\\nUser-provided context: either the .codex-plugin and .cursor-plugin manifests carry a note that hook-based task-state tracking is Claude Code only, or equivalents are built for the harnesses whose payloads support it. Depends on the correlation-key defect, which must be settled first.\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Cross-harness hook documentation review, 2026-09-06\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-09-06\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"0df1a7f910f8d95a889498ddba38a3af80d8fee4e4c12ca013b6b8033b47376b\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABTSBvgg\"}"}